acceptanceCriteria:
AC1 (change-detection, varrido 2026-08-04: RED na main, GREEN na copia patched) - Rodar o install.sh REAL por cima de um ${INSTALL_DIR}/gship que um processo vivo esta executando termina com install rc=0, E o processo vivo sobrevive, E o arquivo deixado em ${INSTALL_DIR}/gship executa com rc=0. A asercao e a CONJUNCAO das tres. Medido na main: install rc=0 e exec rc=137 (SIGKILL, sem diagnostico nenhum). A conjuncao e RED nas duas plataformas por motivos DIFERENTES (macOS envenena a imagem mapeada e o install ainda sai 0; Linux recusa o cp com ETXTBSY e o set -e aborta o install), entao NUNCA escrever asercao de rc=137 so-macOS. Oraculo:
set -uo pipefail
INSTALL_SH="${INSTALL_SH:-$PWD/install.sh}"
[ -r "${INSTALL_SH}" ] || { echo "ORACLE-A FATAL: no readable install.sh at ${INSTALL_SH}"; exit 2; }
command -v bun >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "ORACLE-A FATAL: bun required"; exit 2; }
SCRATCH="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/cam497a.XXXXXX")" || exit 2
FIXPID=""
cleanup() { [ -n "${FIXPID}" ] && kill -9 "${FIXPID}" 2>/dev/null; rm -rf "${SCRATCH}"; return 0; }
trap cleanup EXIT INT TERM
SHIM="${SCRATCH}/shim"; IDIR="${SCRATCH}/install"; SRC="${SCRATCH}/src"
mkdir -p "${SHIM}" "${IDIR}" "${SRC}"
export ORACLE_ASSET="${SCRATCH}/asset" ORACLE_STATE="${SCRATCH}/served" ORACLE_READY="${SCRATCH}/ready"
cat > "${SRC}/fixture.ts" <<'TS'
import { writeFileSync } from "node:fs";
if (process.argv.includes("--stay")) {
	const ready = process.env.ORACLE_READY;
	if (ready) writeFileSync(ready, "ready");
	setTimeout(() => process.exit(0), 600_000);
} else {
	console.log("gship-fixture ok");
}
TS
( cd "${SRC}" && bun build --compile ./fixture.ts --outfile "${ORACLE_ASSET}" ) >"${SCRATCH}/build.log" 2>&1 </dev/null \
	|| { echo "ORACLE-A FATAL: bun build --compile failed:"; cat "${SCRATCH}/build.log"; exit 2; }
if [ "$(uname -s)" = "Darwin" ]; then codesign --force --sign - "${ORACLE_ASSET}" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; fi
"${ORACLE_ASSET}" >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null || { echo "ORACLE-A FATAL: fixture does not run (rc=$?)"; exit 2; }
cp "${ORACLE_ASSET}" "${IDIR}/gship"; chmod +x "${IDIR}/gship"
"${IDIR}/gship" --stay >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null &
FIXPID=$!
i=0; while [ ! -f "${ORACLE_READY}" ] && [ "${i}" -lt 150 ]; do sleep 0.1; i=$((i+1)); done
[ -f "${ORACLE_READY}" ] || { echo "ORACLE-A FATAL: fixture never signalled ready"; exit 2; }
cat > "${SHIM}/curl" <<'SHIM'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
hash_file() { if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sha256sum "$1" | awk '{print $1}'; else shasum -a 256 "$1" | awk '{print $1}'; fi; }
URL=""; OUT=""; prev=""
for arg in "$@"; do
	if [[ "${prev}" == "-o" ]]; then OUT="${arg}"; elif [[ "${arg}" != -* ]]; then URL="${arg}"; fi
	prev="${arg}"
done
if [[ "${URL}" == *SHA256SUMS.txt* ]]; then
	printf '%s  %s\n' "$(cat "${ORACLE_STATE}.hash")" "$(cat "${ORACLE_STATE}.name")" > "${OUT}"; exit 0
fi
if [[ -n "${OUT}" ]]; then
	cp "${ORACLE_ASSET}" "${OUT}"; basename "${URL}" > "${ORACLE_STATE}.name"; hash_file "${OUT}" > "${ORACLE_STATE}.hash"; exit 0
fi
echo '[{"tag_name": "v0.0.0-oracle"}]'; exit 0
SHIM
chmod +x "${SHIM}/curl"
PATH="${SHIM}:${PATH}" GATESHIP_VERSION="v0.0.0-oracle" GATESHIP_INSTALL_DIR="${IDIR}" \
	bash "${INSTALL_SH}" >"${SCRATCH}/install.log" 2>&1 </dev/null
INSTALL_RC=$?
FAILED=0
fail() { echo "  ASSERT FAIL: $*"; FAILED=1; }
[ "${INSTALL_RC}" -eq 0 ] || fail "install.sh exited ${INSTALL_RC}, expected 0 (Linux: ETXTBSY under set -e)"
kill -0 "${FIXPID}" 2>/dev/null || fail "live process pid ${FIXPID} did not survive the install"
"${IDIR}/gship" >/dev/null 2>&1 </dev/null
EXEC_RC=$?
[ "${EXEC_RC}" -eq 0 ] || fail "INSTALL_DIR/gship exec rc=${EXEC_RC}, expected 0 (137 = SIGKILL, poisoned image)"
if [ "${FAILED}" -eq 0 ]; then echo "ORACLE-A GREEN (install rc=0, pid alive, exec rc=0)"; exit 0; fi
echo "ORACLE-A RED (install rc=${INSTALL_RC}, exec rc=${EXEC_RC})"; exit 1

AC3 (change-detection, varrido 2026-08-04: RED na main, GREEN na copia patched) - No install.sh nenhum cp escreve direto em ${DEST} e nenhum rm apaga ${DEST}; a unica escrita em ${DEST} e um mv. Este pin existe para fechar uma lacuna que AC1 e AC2 PROVADAMENTE nao enxergam: um conserto por 'rm -f ${DEST}; cp' passa nos dois (mata o SIGKILL e produz inode novo) e ainda assim deixa a janela de leitura parcial que e o segundo sintoma do issue. Especie declarada: pin estrutural, e ele e estrutural porque a propriedade em disputa E qual syscall faz a troca, nao um comportamento observavel sem corrida. Oraculo:
# ORACLE-C: install.sh swaps DEST by rename, never by a cp/rm+cp onto DEST.
S="${INSTALL_SH:-install.sh}"
grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*cp[[:space:]].*"\$\{DEST\}"[[:space:]]*$' "$S" && { echo "RED: a cp still writes directly to \${DEST}"; exit 1; }
grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*rm[[:space:]].*"\$\{DEST\}"' "$S" && { echo "RED: rm on \${DEST} present (rm+cp leaves the torn-read window)"; exit 1; }
grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*mv[[:space:]].*"\$\{DEST\}"[[:space:]]*$' "$S" || { echo "RED: no mv whose destination is \${DEST}"; exit 1; }
echo "GREEN"; exit 0
